.TH KEXPAND 1 "2026-07-14" "kexpand 0.2.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kexpand \- expand SUSE kernel-source patches into a Linux kernel git repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kexpand
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kexpand
reads the \fIseries.conf\fR patch list and \fIrpm/config.sh\fR base-version
declaration from a SUSE kernel-source.git working tree, applies every
non-guarded patch to an in-memory file state, and writes one git commit
per patch into the output repository.
.PP
The output repository is initialised with a git alternates link pointing at
the upstream Linux git clone, so only new blobs, trees, and commits are stored
locally; all upstream objects are shared read-only.
.PP
With
.B \-\-one-shot
a single squashed commit is written instead, containing only the final state
of all modified files.  This is significantly faster but loses per-patch
history.
.PP
.B kexpand
must be run from the root of the kernel-source.git checkout, unless the
.B \-C
option is used to specify the directory explicitly.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <OUTPUT>
Path to the output git repository.  The directory is created and
\fBgit init\fR is run if it does not already exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " BRANCH" ", \-\-branch " BRANCH
Name of the branch to create or update in the output repository.
Default: \fBmaster\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l " LINUX" ", \-\-linux " LINUX
Path to the upstream linux git clone (read-only access is sufficient).
May also be supplied via the environment variable
.BR LINUX_GIT .
Either this option or
.B LINUX_GIT
is required.
.TP
.BI \-C " DIR" ", \-\-directory " DIR
Change to
.I DIR
before doing anything, analogous to
.BR "make \-C" .
Without this option,
.B kexpand
must be run from the kernel-source.git working tree root.
.TP
.BI \-j " JOBS" ", \-\-jobs " JOBS
Number of threads for parallel patch parsing.
.B 0
(the default) lets rayon choose automatically based on available CPUs.
.TP
.BI "\-\-max-fuzz " FUZZ
Maximum context-line fuzz allowed when matching patch hunks.
Default: \fB2\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-failed
Warn and skip patches that fail to apply instead of aborting.
A diagnostic line is printed to stderr for each skipped patch.
.TP
.B \-v ", \-\-verbose"
Print the path of each patch as it is applied.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Read, parse, and apply all patches in memory but skip writing any git output.
Useful for testing patch applicability without creating the output repository.
.TP
.B \-q ", \-\-quiet"
Suppress all progress output.
.TP
.B \-R ", \-\-no-repack"
Skip the final pack-merge step.  The output repository will contain multiple
pack files (blob shards plus a commit pack).  Saves roughly 0.6 s; mainly
useful for debugging or when a subsequent
.B git gc
is planned.
.TP
.BI "\-\-blob-shards " N
Number of parallel
.B git fast-import
processes used for writing blob objects.
.B 0
(the default) means min(available CPUs, 16).
.TP
.B \-1 ", \-\-one-shot"
Apply all patches to the in-memory tree and emit a single squashed commit
containing the final state of each modified file.  Much faster than the
default one-commit-per-patch mode, but the resulting repository has no
per-patch history.
.TP
.B \-h ", \-\-help"
Print help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LINUX_GIT
Path to the upstream linux git clone.  Used as the value of
.B \-\-linux
when that option is not given on the command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B series.conf
Ordered list of patches to apply.  Read from the kernel-source working tree
root (or the directory given by
.BR \-C ).
Its presence is also used to validate that the working directory is correct.
.TP
.B rpm/config.sh
Searched for a \fBSRCVERSION=\fR line that identifies the upstream kernel
release tag (e.g.\& \fBSRCVERSION=6.4\fR maps to git tag \fBv6.4\fR).
.TP
.IB OUTPUT "/.git/objects/info/alternates"
Written by
.B kexpand
to link the output repository to the upstream linux clone's object store.
.TP
.IB OUTPUT "/.git/objects/pack/pack-*.{pack,idx}"
Pack files produced by
.BR kexpand .
Merged into a single pack at the end of the run unless
.B \-R
is used.
.SH SERIES.CONF SYNTAX
Each non-blank line of
.I series.conf
is interpreted as follows:
.TP
.RI "Leading " # " (after optional whitespace)"
Comment — skipped.
.TP
.RI "Leading " + " or " \-
Guarded — skipped unconditionally.
.TP
Otherwise
Applied — the first whitespace-separated token is the patch file path
relative to the kernel-source working tree root.
.PP
Patches are applied with strip level 1 (\fBpatch \-p1\fR).
.SH COMMIT FORMAT
In the default (one commit per patch) mode each commit records:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBauthor\fR: from the patch's \fBFrom:\fR (name and email) and \fBDate:\fR
(RFC\ 2822) headers.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcommitter\fR: \fBkexpand <kexpand@localhost>\fR with the current UTC time.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBsubject\fR: from the patch's \fBSubject:\fR header with any
\fB[PATCH\ ...]\fR prefix stripped.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBbody\fR: the description text between the RFC\ 2822 headers and the
\fB\-\-\-\fR separator.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBtrailers\fR appended to the body when present: \fBReferences:\fR,
\fBPatch-mainline:\fR, \fBGit-commit:\fR, \fBGit-repo:\fR, \fBAlt-commit:\fR,
and an \fBOriginal-patch:\fR trailer with the relative patch file path.
.PP
In
.B \-\-one-shot
mode a single commit is written with author and committer set to
.B "kexpand <kexpand@localhost>"
and subject \fBApply N SUSE kernel patches\fR.
.SH NOTES
Binary patches (\fBGIT binary patch\fR or \fBbinary\fR metadata) are silently
skipped; a diagnostic line is printed to stderr.
.PP
Typical performance on SLE15-SP7 (60,888 patches) with a warm page cache on a
16-core AMD Ryzen AI 7 PRO:
.RS
.PD 0
.TP 32
Default (one commit per patch)
~22 s
.TP
.B \-R
(skip repack) ~21 s
.TP
.B \-1
(one-shot, single commit) ~5 s
.TP
.B "\-1 \-R"
~4 s
.PD
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Expand all non-guarded patches from the SLE15-SP7 branch of a
kernel-source checkout into a new output repository:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd ~/kernel/suse/kernel-source
git checkout SLE15-SP7
kexpand \-\-linux ~/git/linux ~/git/suse-expanded \-\-branch SLE15-SP7
.fi
.RE
.PP
Same operation without changing the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git \-C ~/kernel/suse/kernel-source checkout SLE15-SP7
kexpand \-C ~/kernel/suse/kernel-source \e
        \-\-linux ~/git/linux       \e
        ~/git/suse-expanded        \e
        \-\-branch SLE15-SP7
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fastest mode — single squashed commit, no per-patch history:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kexpand \-C ~/kernel/suse/kernel-source \e
        \-\-linux ~/git/linux           \e
        ~/git/suse-expanded            \e
        \-\-branch SLE15-SP7            \e
        \-\-one-shot
.fi
.RE
.PP
Test patch applicability without writing any git objects:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kexpand \-C ~/kernel/suse/kernel-source \e
        \-\-linux ~/git/linux           \e
        /tmp/throwaway                 \e
        \-\-dry-run
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-fast-import (1),
.BR patch (1),
.BR quilt (1)
